{
  "$comment": "Fingerprints of every sample in test-output/samples/ (written by the BUILT server, scripts/generate-samples.ts). Regenerate deliberately with `npx tsx scripts/verify-samples.ts --update`, and say why in the release notes: a changed hash means existing output changed. Mode `bytes` is a SHA-256 of the file (every archive written over pinned inputs: DOS-epoch default timestamps, explicit dates written in UTC, canonical layout); mode `semantic` is a SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of the result without its volatile members (filePath, outputDir: absolute paths into a temporary sandbox) and with its host members neutralised (the core count of describe_engine.capabilities, the Node / OS lines of a governance draft and the sizeBytes that measures them: the baseline is made on one machine and held on every CI runner). Each entry's `since` names the release whose output the hash is: it is carried forward untouched while the sample is unchanged, and moves to the release doing the rebaseline when the hash changes, so the chain 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0 -> … stays auditable and every re-anchoring is visible in the diff.",
  "baselineVersion": "1.1.0",
  "provenance": "1.0.0 baseline: captured on 2026-10-18 from the v1.0.0 tree (commit 144af6d, zipnative 1.0.0, @modelcontextprotocol/server 2.0.0) before any 1.1.0 change, by running every examples/*.json through the built server under TZ=UTC over the frozen inputs of tests/fixtures/examples/ (pinned by tests/fixtures/SHA256SUMS). Under TZ=UTC the 1.0.0 engine wrote DOS fields from UTC, so these hashes are also what 1.1.0 must write on every host once dosTimeMode: 'utc' is pinned; an entry that moves to a later since is a deliberate rebaseline explained in that release's notes. 1.1.0 rebaseline (2026-10-18, zipnative 1.1.0, @modelcontextprotocol/server 2.3.1): 39 of the 41 1.0.0 samples are byte- or structure-identical and keep since 1.0.0; describe-engine.json moves to since 1.1.0 because it reports the new version, the fourth ceiling, codecs[].incremental and the new unexposed rows; draft-governance-issue.json moves because its environment block quotes the package version; the 13 samples of the new 1.1.0 examples (canonicalize, merge, Zip64 streaming, determinism report, extended timestamps, byte ranges, compact canonical) join with since 1.1.0 (release-notes/v1.1.0.md, Upgrade). Audit fix (B-032, 2026-10-18): examples/draft-governance-issue.json now drafts a wrapper feature request instead of a known engine limitation, so draft-governance-issue.json was re-anchored again at 1.1.0. CI-001 (2026-10-20): the first CI run of the 1.1.0 branch failed on every runner because the draft result's sizeBytes measures the markdown, host lines included (5004 B on the Windows host of the baseline, 5025 B on ubuntu-latest); the semantic projection now neutralises sizeBytes next to a draftMarkdown, and draft-governance-issue.json keeps since 1.1.0 (the projection changed, the output did not).",
